      "assessment": "All1572 lines read, including substantive DDC custody and scheduler-order tests. Seven-act controller binds candidate bytes/checker observations, requires configured DDC sinks to expose the tape, snapshots exact prefix and rejects any changed prefix/presence before persistence. This is stronger than length-only mirror checks. Higher-carrier remeasurement refuses decreases in either exact obstruction statistic under the declared lift assumptions. However ground_truth_admissible=false skips post-lift measurement while later audit hashes use the lifted carrier, leaving old measurement versus new carrier binding dependent on that caller policy. Scheduler finalization synthesizes fixed PASS/changed_state1 and a hard-coded work-packet ID, precharges seven steps with saturating subtraction, and trusts an optional initial_state without local packet identity validation. Scheduler/scene owners still need assessment before end-to-end conclusions. Publication failure is explicitly retained separately without changing task outcome and strips receipt pins; no retained ports run. Inline test/mutation comments are source evidence only.",
