      "assessment": "Council assembly reads YAML string-keyed maps, rejects normalized seat-name collisions, builds finite seat/scene/transition/plan records and hashes both original YAML bodies with domain and length framing. Input scenes are checked only for ten unique normalized IDs; their contents are otherwise discarded in favor of compiled layout. Core-seat insert uses or_insert, so an existing same-ID declaration with a different inferred trust domain is retained: one-seat-per-trust-domain wording is not locally enforced. Roles are inferred by substrings/iterable acts, independence lists are empty, and the generated license hash is a proposal identity, not an authenticated capability. Core mode transparently maps seatless acts to the evaluator; full wrapper intentionally retains legacy full mode. Prefix plus exact count-template transfer; no YAML loader/scheduler execution.",
