      "assessment": "RecordingSeatPort adds reviewed plan/guidance and explicitly untrusted historical scene observations before computing request digest; scene context has64-record/64KiB caps. A configured journal must append SeatTurnStarted before the inner call, but checkpoint failures merely accumulate residuals and missing journal is an admitted mode. Returned replies with a supplied mismatching request digest are rejected; absent reply digest is accepted, so response binding is conditional on the concrete port. Reply/raw bytes and failure paths are preserved in turn records, interruption resumes unwinding with pending state for recovery, and completed-journal failure is reported separately. Prefix fully read plus exact count-template trailer; no seat/journal/provider invocation.",
